---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const temples = await getCollection('temples');
const verified = temples.filter((t) => t.data.status === 'verified').length;
const pending = temples.length - verified;
---
<Base title="About" description="Why this directory exists and how its accuracy standard works.">
  <div class="wrap prose-page">
    <h1>About Sanatana Kshetras</h1>
    <p>
      Sanatana Kshetras is a comprehensive, git-based directory of Hindu / Sanatana Dharma
      temples across India and the globe — built so pilgrims can plan a visit, and so podcasters,
      monks, and researchers have a well-sourced starting point for a story.
    </p>

    <h2>Verified vs. pending</h2>
    <p>
      Of {temples.length} temples, {verified} are marked <strong>verified</strong> — corroborated
      by at least one independently checkable source — and {pending} are marked
      <strong>pending</strong>, meaning something about the entry (a date, a founding legend, a
      precise location) could not yet be independently confirmed. Pending doesn't mean wrong; it
      means honest about what's still uncertain. Every entry with unresolved questions carries
      explicit <em>review flags</em> describing exactly what's unconfirmed, rather than smoothing
      the uncertainty over.
    </p>

    <h2>Documented history vs. oral tradition</h2>
    <p>
      Every entry marks its history as <strong>documented</strong> (independently attested),
      <strong>legend</strong> (oral or scriptural tradition, not independently verifiable), or
      <strong>mixed</strong> — and every source is cited by type: scripture, oral tradition, or
      historical record.
    </p>

    <h2>The data is public and versioned</h2>
    <p>
      Nothing here lives in a private database. Every temple is a Markdown file in a public
      GitHub repository, validated against a published schema, with its full edit history
      visible. See <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}contribute/`}>Contribute</a> for how to
      add or correct an entry.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .prose-page { padding-block: 2rem 3rem; max-width: 42rem; }
</style>
